{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3057","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3057","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3057\",\"parent_revision\":\"777dabb2c668e3307284fc27a0bfed5c1787284d7d8d5b93575e3a3d2a648812\",\"root_revision\":\"777dabb2c668e3307284fc27a0bfed5c1787284d7d8d5b93575e3a3d2a648812\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe default item-read path builds its own section directory, pagination, and content slicing instead of using the markdown engine. An inventory found 14 bypass points and roughly 430 lines of hand-rolled markdown logic, including the same section-index format built independently in three separate functions.\\n\\nThe hand-built index emits a bracket-numbered scheme addressing only top-level sections, cannot paginate, and does not match the engine's addresses. Requirement R1 forbids a second implementation regardless of whether it works.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] The default read path returns results produced by the engine, not hand-built strings\\n- [ ] The bracket-numbered index is gone; addresses returned are the engine's dot-path scheme\\n- [ ] The section directory paginates when it exceeds budget, per R2\\n- [ ] The grooming validation gate reads section presence from the engine and passes\\n- [ ] The three duplicate index builders are deleted, not left unreferenced\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- Intended behaviour is defined in `plugins/development-harness/docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md`. Component ownership is defined in `plugins/development-harness/docs/component-architecture.md`. Parent: #3054.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Sequencing Constraint\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe structures marked for deletion are what the grooming validation gate currently reads to check section presence. That gate must be rewritten to read from the engine before these are removed, or grooming breaks.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"2fc7e8c3e555284749b4fd448480dc742fd72a8799a1276e9d57dd2734438a38\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPvb0QQ\"}"}